<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#maincontent">Skip to main content</a>

  <main id="maincontent" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Cat care guide</p>
      <h1 id="page-title">Frequently asked questions about cats</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        Practical answers about cat behavior, care, and health, presented in a simple FAQ that starts collapsed and opens one answer at a time when you choose.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-list" aria-label="Cat FAQ">
      <div class="example">
        <h2>
          <button class="question-button" type="button" id="question-1" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-1">
            Why do cats purr?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="answer-1" aria-labelledby="question-1">
          <p>Cats often purr when they feel safe and content, but they may also purr to soothe themselves when stressed or recovering. <strong>Purring is a signal with context</strong>, so body language matters too.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h2>
          <button class="question-button" type="button" id="question-2" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-2">
            How often should I feed an adult cat?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="answer-2" aria-labelledby="question-2">
          <p>Most healthy adult cats do well with measured meals once or twice a day, though the right amount depends on age, activity level, and the food itself. Fresh water should always be available, and your veterinarian can help fine-tune portions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h2>
          <button class="question-button" type="button" id="question-3" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-3">
            Why does my cat knead blankets and laps?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="answer-3" aria-labelledby="question-3">
          <p>Kneading is a common comfort behavior that starts in kittenhood. Many cats keep doing it when they feel relaxed, warm, or attached to a person, so it usually reflects contentment rather than a problem.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h2>
          <button class="question-button" type="button" id="question-4" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-4">
            How can I help a cat feel comfortable in a new home?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="answer-4" aria-labelledby="question-4">
          <p>Start with one quiet room stocked with food, water, a litter box, hiding spots, and a scratching surface. Let the cat explore at its own pace and keep routines predictable while trust builds.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h2>
          <button class="question-button" type="button" id="question-5" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-5">
            When should I call a veterinarian?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="answer-5" aria-labelledby="question-5">
          <p>Reach out promptly if your cat stops eating, struggles to breathe, vomits repeatedly, hides suddenly, or shows major changes in litter box habits. Regular wellness visits are also important, even when your cat seems healthy.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    const faqButtons = document.querySelectorAll(".question-button");

    faqButtons.forEach((button) => {
      const details = document.getElementById(button.getAttribute("aria-controls"));
      button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
      details.hidden = true;

      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const isExpanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
        details.hidden = isExpanded;
      });
    });

    document.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
      if (event.key !== "Escape") {
        return;
      }

      const activeExample = document.activeElement.closest(".example");
      if (!activeExample) {
        return;
      }

      const button = activeExample.querySelector(".question-button");
      const details = activeExample.querySelector(".details");

      if (button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") !== "true") {
        return;
      }

      button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
      details.hidden = true;
      button.focus();
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
