          <p>Kneading is a common comfort behavior that starts in kittenhood. Many cats keep doing it when they feel relaxed, warm, or attached to a person, so it usually reflects contentment rather than a problem.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <h2>
          <button class="question-button" type="button" id="question-4" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-4">
            How can I help a cat feel comfortable in a new home?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div class="details" id="answer-4" aria-labelledby="question-4">
          <p>Start with one quiet room stocked with food, water, a litter box, hiding spots, and a scratching surface. Let the cat explore at its own pace and keep routines predictable while trust builds.</p>
